    "title": "Sysop Wiki",
    "text": "Sysop Wiki A practical guide to running your Spitfire-X bulletin board. Find a setting or a task. The Windows and Linux configuration reference explains each setting, new-entry defaults, saved choices, limits and Save behavior. The operating guides continue to grow. Search for the label you see in SFXConfig, or choose a topic below. Using Linux SFXConfig? Find any of its 33 pages , with the normal task and save scope for each. Find your task 01 Get your BBS ready Install SFX, name your BBS and get ready for callers. 02 Run your BBS each day Start and stop your BBS, change settings and watch caller activity. 03 Manage callers and chat Accounts, access, limits and Sysop chat. 04 Messages and offline mail Message areas, local mail, QWK/REP and NetMail. 05 Files and transfers File areas, File Manager and upload scanning. 06 Add and maintain Doors Door entries, menus, paths and drop files. 07 Connect to FTN networks Networks, message-area links and mail exchange. 08 Maintain, back up and recover Scheduled jobs, logs, backups and BBS Health Check. 09 Update SFX and solve problems Updates, repair, troubleshooting and problem reports. 10 Customization & Displays Display filenames, artwork, codes, colors and a practical test sheet . External BinkD The 1.0.0b2 test packages include External BinkD support. Read setup and daily use and the exact supported profile reference . Thanks to People and projects behind Spitfire-X . Using this wiki Choose a topic from the contents or search the pages already here. You can read and search without an Internet connection. Your browser's Find command searches the page you have open. The short README.txt on Windows or readme.txt on Linux is the starting point for this release. Keep this wiki and its supporting files together when moving your SFX folder."
